{"id":28085,"path":"/vocabulary/a1/shops-and-shopping-a1-english-vocabulary/","parentId":26178,"order":90,"section":"vocabulary","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Shops and shopping – A1 English Vocabulary","seo":{"title":"Shops and shopping – A1 English Vocabulary - Test-English","description":"Learn words for types of shops and useful shopping phrases with this Elementary Vocabulary lesson with pictures, examples, exercises & games!","image":"/media/uploads/A1-English-Vocabulary_Shops-shopping.jpg"},"modified":"2023-11-25T10:50:14","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h2>Shops and shopping</h2> <p>In this A1 Elementary <a href=\"/vocabulary\">Vocabulary</a> Lesson, you will learn different common types of shops and useful phrases that are used when shopping. Check the explanation to learn the words and then do the exercises.</p> <h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct option for each gap.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"1047\"></div>","<h2>Shops and shopping</h2> <h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Complete each sentence with one of the options. You can use each option only ONCE.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"1048\"></div>","<h2>Shops and shopping</h2> <h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete each sentence with the correct ending. You can choose each option ONLY ONCE.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"1049\"></div>","<h2>Shops and shopping</h2> <h3>Exercise 4</h3> <h5>Match the sentences/pictures with the terms.</h5> <p></p> <h6>Reload the page to play again.<br> Here’s a link to our <a href=\"https://quizlet.com/es/855397092/shops-and-shopping-a1-vocabulary-flash-cards/\">Quizlet study set</a> about Shops and Shopping.</h6>"],"explanation":"<h2>Shops and Shopping</h2> <p>In this A1 Elementary <a href=\"/vocabulary\">Vocabulary</a> Lesson, you will learn different common types of shops and useful phrases that are used when shopping. Check the pictures and read the definitions and examples below.</p> <p><img src=\"/media/uploads/Shops-shopping_A1-vocabulary.webp\" alt=\"Collage of various types of retail shops for A1 English Vocabulary lesson on Shops and Shopping.\" width=\"500\" height=\"828\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-28383\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">1</span> A <strong>grocery store</strong> is a shop where you buy food and things for the house.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">2</span> A <strong>bakery</strong> is a place where you buy bread, cakes, and pastries.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">3</span> A <strong>chemist’s</strong> (UK) or <strong>pharmacy</strong> (US) is a shop where you get medicine and health products.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">4</span> A <strong>clothing/clothes store</strong> (US) or <strong>clothes shop</strong> (UK) is a shop where you buy outfits like shirts and trousers.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">5</span> A <strong>shoe store</strong> is a place where you can buy footwear for your feet.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">6</span> A <strong>bookstore</strong> (US)&nbsp;is a shop with lots of books to read and buy.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">7</span> A <strong>toy store</strong> is a shop that sells toys and games for children.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">8</span> A <strong>hardware store</strong> or <strong>DIY shop</strong> (UK) is a shop where you find tools and things for fixing your house.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">9</span> An <strong>electronics store</strong> is a place to buy things like computers and TVs.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">10</span> A <strong>jewelry store</strong> (US) or <strong>jewellery shop</strong> (UK) is a shop where you can buy rings, necklaces, and other pretty things to wear.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">11</span> A <strong>flower shop</strong> or <strong>florist</strong> is a place where you buy flowers for decoration or as gifts.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">12</span> A <strong>pet store</strong> is a shop where you find animals like cats and dogs and things for them.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">13</span> A <strong>corner shop</strong> (UK) or a <strong>convenience store</strong> (US) is a small shop where you buy everyday items such as newspapers, magazines, snacks, drinks, and some food items.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">14</span> A <strong>stationer’s</strong> (UK) or <strong>stationery store</strong> (US) is a place where you buy things for writing and office work like pens and paper.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">15</span> A <strong>furniture store</strong> is a big shop where you buy things like chairs, tables, and beds for your home.</p> <p><span class=\"numPink\">16</span> A <strong>gift shop</strong> is a shop where you find things to buy as presents for people.</p> <h3>Differences between the UK and the US</h3> <p>The names of shops are often different in the US and the UK. For example, in the US, they normally use the word <strong>store</strong> to refer to shops. In the UK, the word <strong>shop</strong> is more common. Compare:</p> <div class=\"tg-wrap\"> <table class=\"tg\"> <thead> <tr> <th>The United States</th> <th>The United Kingdom</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>clothing store</td> <td>clothes shop</td> </tr> <tr> <td>shoe store</td> <td>shoe shop</td> </tr> <tr> <td>bookstore</td> <td>bookshop</td> </tr> <tr> <td>toy store</td> <td>toy shop</td> </tr> <tr> <td>jewelry store</td> <td>jewellery shop</td> </tr> <tr> <td>pet store</td> <td>pet shop</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> <h2>Useful English phrases when shopping</h2> <p>Here’s some useful language that you can use when you are shopping.</p> <div class=\"tg-wrap\"> <table class=\"tg\"> <thead> <tr> <th>Shop assistant</th> <th>Customer</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>How can I help you?</td> <td>I’m just looking, thanks.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Here you are.</td> <td>I’m looking for…</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Sure./Of course.</td> <td>Do you have any…?</td> </tr> <tr> <td>It’s … pounds/dollars.</td> <td>How much is it?</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Here’s your change (and your receipt).</td> <td>How much is/are the…?</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Here’s your receipt.</td> <td>I’ll pay in cash/by credit card.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Have a nice day.</td> <td>Can I pay in cash/by credit card?</td> </tr> <tr> <td>And here’s your bag.</td> <td>Can I try this on?</td> </tr> <tr> <td></td> <td>Do you have this in… (blue/a large/etc.)?</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> <h3>Listen &amp; Practice: Vocabulary with Pronunciation</h3> <p>Here’s a video to help you review the vocabulary from this lesson and improve your pronunciation.</p> <div class=\"video-container\"> <div class=\"embed-container\"><div data-youtube=\"cl-OzpKbY3c\"></div></div> </div> <div class=\"separator-dots\"><span>Flashcards</span></div> <p>After completing the exercises in this lesson on Shops and Shopping, you can use the unit’s <a href=\"https://quizlet.com/855397092\">Vocabulary Flashcards</a> to revise and help you memorize the terms.</p>","quizzes":[{"id":1047,"questions":[{"id":8945,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I bought a new television from the _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":15811,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> electronics store</span>"},{"id":15812,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> newsagent’s</span>"},{"id":15813,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> stationery store</span>"},{"id":15814,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> pharmacy</span>"}]},{"id":8946,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The _____ at the end of the street sells lots of pens and notebooks.</div>","choices":[{"id":15815,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> pharmacy</span>"},{"id":15816,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> toy store</span>"},{"id":15817,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> stationery store</span>"},{"id":15818,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> pet store</span>"}]},{"id":8947,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Tom bought his wife some roses from the _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":15819,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> hardware store</span>"},{"id":15820,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> electronics store</span>"},{"id":15821,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> flower shop</span>"},{"id":15822,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> shoe store</span>"}]},{"id":8948,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Alice bought a pair of boots from the _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":15823,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> pet shop</span>"},{"id":15824,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> shoe store</span>"},{"id":15825,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> chemist’s</span>"},{"id":15826,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> hardware store</span>"}]},{"id":8949,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I could smell fresh bread when I walked past the _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":15827,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> shoe store</span>"},{"id":15828,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> chemist’s</span>"},{"id":15829,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> gift shop</span>"},{"id":15830,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> bakery</span>"}]},{"id":8950,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I saw lots of beautiful necklaces at the _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":15831,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> jewelry store</span>"},{"id":15832,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> chemist’s</span>"},{"id":15833,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> hardware store</span>"},{"id":15834,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> electronics store</span>"}]},{"id":8951,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I’m going to the _____ to buy some cheese.</div>","choices":[{"id":15835,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> electronics shop</span>"},{"id":15836,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> flower shop</span>"},{"id":15837,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> grocery store</span>"},{"id":15838,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> pet store</span>"}]},{"id":8952,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I bought a beautiful golden fish at the _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":15839,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> hardware store</span>"},{"id":15840,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> pet store</span>"},{"id":15841,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> supermarket</span>"},{"id":15842,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> flower shop</span>"}]},{"id":8953,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We went to the _____ to buy some pills.</div>","choices":[{"id":15843,"letter":"A.","html":"